From 91f5ffe185f0cd16b23462a32b6e02a3b9516c61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Alani <mikealanni@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:04:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] feat(qwen38-flash-next): token-history drafting and a
 draft confidence gate

Drafting from the token history is a retrieval guess over tokens the session
already holds: when the context ends in a phrase that occurred earlier, the
tokens that followed it replace the MTP chain for that cycle. The target still
verifies every token, so a wrong guess only costs the verify width. A repeated
phrase says nothing about the predictor's acceptance, so these cycles stay out
of its adaptive length controller.

The gate stops before a speculative slot the draft head is unlikely to win.
Verification is unchanged, so it only gives up positions.

No environment switches. History drafting closes #239.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
